# T-1743: transitive abandoned bindings.
# Binding 'a' is defined in the first intermediate body.
# Binding 'b' references 'a' in the second intermediate body.
# Neither 'a' nor 'b' is referenced from the final expression (42).
# The transitive analysis detects both as unreachable.
[call [fn [let x] [a: [+ x 1]] [b: [+ a 2]] 42] 10]
=== out
Int(42)

=== warn
variable 'a' is never referenced
